# Long-lived caching is only safe for files whose name changes when their
# contents do. The Webflow bundle and jQuery are content-hashed by the
# exporter (webflow.schunk.6d83011aa4f34449.js), and images are replaced
# rather than edited in place, so both can be pinned for a year.
#
# The stylesheets are the exception: style.css and watch.css keep the same
# name forever, so "immutable" pins whatever a visitor cached first and no
# later edit ever reaches them. That has already silently swallowed CSS
# changes in four separate rounds now — two other PRs, and then this same
# repo's own active-development commits landing five times in a row without
# anyone (including the author) remembering to bump ?v=. A max-age, even a
# short one, has the same failure mode at a shorter delay: it still trusts
# a stale copy for the whole window, and the fix depends on a human
# remembering a manual step every single time CSS changes — which is
# exactly the step that kept getting missed.
#
# no-cache (the name is misleading — it still caches the body) removes that
# dependency entirely: every load sends a conditional request and gets
# either a 304 off an unmodified file — cheap, no re-download — or the
# actual new bytes if it changed. There is no window where a visitor can be
# served content older than what's actually deployed, and ?v= stops being
# something anyone has to remember.
#
# These rules are written to not overlap. A single /assets/* rule plus a
# narrower /assets/css/* rule would leave two Cache-Control headers matching
# the same request, and which one wins is not worth depending on.

/assets/css/*
  Cache-Control: public, no-cache

/assets/images/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Unlike style.css/watch.css above, these names are safe to mark immutable:
# font bytes essentially never change once deployed, and there's no ?v= on
# these URLs to bump either way. If a font ever genuinely needs replacing,
# rename the file (add a version suffix) rather than overwriting in place —
# the same reason the Webflow bundle above is content-hashed.
/assets/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/assets/animate/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/favicon.ico
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000

/*.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
